@startuml
!include ../../common/eztrade-style.puml

title EZTrade - Dependencias logicas Spring Modulith

package "Spring Modulith application" {
  component "user\n@ApplicationModule" as User EZ_BACKEND
  component "security\npermitido: user :: api" as Security EZ_BACKEND
  component "market\n@ApplicationModule" as Market EZ_BACKEND
  component "trading\npermitido: market :: api" as Trading EZ_BACKEND
  component "wallet\npermitido: trading :: events,\nuser :: api" as Wallet EZ_BACKEND
  component "portfolio\npermitido: trading :: events,\nwallet :: events,\nmarket :: api" as Portfolio EZ_BACKEND
  component "notifications\npermitido: trading :: events,\nportfolio :: events,\nwallet :: events" as Notifications EZ_BACKEND
}

Security --> User : LoadUserForSecurityPort\nUserOwnerLookup via api
Trading --> Market : MarketPriceLookupPort\ncurrentPrice(symbol)
Portfolio --> Market : MarketPriceLookupPort\nvaluation
Wallet --> User : UserOwnerLookupPort\ntransfer recipient lookup

Trading ..> Wallet : OrderPlacedEvent\nOrderCancelledEvent\nOrderExecutionRequestEvent
Wallet ..> Trading : OrderExecutedEvent\n(after settlement)
Trading ..> Portfolio : OrderExecutedEvent
Wallet ..> Portfolio : AvailableCashUpdatedEvent
Trading ..> Notifications : eventos de orden
Wallet ..> Notifications : InsufficientFundsEvent
Portfolio ..> Notifications : PortfolioValuationUpdatedEvent

note bottom
Evidencia: los ficheros package-info.java declaran allowedDependencies.
ModulithStructureTest verifica el grafo de modulos durante la fase de pruebas.
Las flechas continuas representan dependencias directas de puertos/API; las discontinuas representan eventos de dominio Spring.
end note

@enduml
